          A dehumidifier is the single most useful long-term tool against silverfish, and it will not get rid of them on its own. Silverfish depend on humid air, and taking the humidity away turns a comfortable habitat into a hostile one. But adults can live for months without food and survive dry spells in sheltered spots, so the machine slowly squeezes them out rather than wiping them out. Pair it with the steps below and the problem goes away; rely on it alone and you will still be seeing them next spring.
